## this is meant to teach C

Quite naturally.
You will eventually need:

- fixed-width integers (`uint8_t`, `uint16_t`, etc.)
- bit manipulation
- pointers
- structs
- unions
- arrays
- memory layout
- `volatile`
- function pointers
- file I/O
- binary parsing
- command-line arguments
- perhaps `ncurses` or SDL for the UI
- eventually ELF parsing

And unlike doing random C exercises, **every C concept has a reason to exist.**

keep the first milestone extremely small — **"execute 10 AVR instructions and visualize GPIO"**
